13:30:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Alamosa  Vicinity/Central San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Southern San Luis Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9142e8d63f961ff030cf12d7bfb87684241d5c39.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9142e8d63f961ff030cf12d7bfb87684241d5c39.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued September 14 at 12:39PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 1238 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near\nCrestone Peak, or 33 miles northeast of Alamosa, moving east at 30\nmph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nCrestone Peak and Great Sand Dunes.","ends":"2026-09-14T13:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Del Norte Vicinity/Northern San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Northern Sangre de Cristo Mountains Between 8500 And 11000 Ft; Northern Sangre de Cristo Mountains above 11000 Ft; Wet Mountain Valley Below 8500 Ft; Walsenburg Vicinity/Upper Huerfano River Basin Below 7500 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8a2412c72e6b091f8e515f8b3691608953f0967f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8a2412c72e6b091f8e515f8b3691608953f0967f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-09-14T17:50:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 141750 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1150 AM MDT Mon Sep 14 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - One last hot day today, cooling off for Tuesday and through the end of the work week after a cold front arrives. - Increasing shower and thunderstorm coverage, especially Wednesday through Friday, with increasing flash flood risk on area burn scars. && .SHORT TER","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"of